    {
      "id": "midnight_butter_bread_at_mushroom_house",
      "title": "Midnight Butter Bread At Mushroom House",
      "description": "In a quiet corner of a Berlin park, without an address or street number, stands an invisible Mushroom House where a little girl lives with her ancient horse spirit. They spend their days playing with mathematics and syntax, discovering the peculiar pleasures of thinking together. During a rainy November week, they decide to bake a round golden butter bread, but yeast, the moodiest of ingredients, makes them uncertain whether their dough will ever rise. They discuss temperatures, liquids, proportions, and procedures, applying all their mathematical wisdom to the mysterious behaviour of living dough. Finally, at midnight, there is nothing left to calculate, so the little girl sits beside her old horse, resting her small hands in his great hooves, while the stone oven quietly does its work. By morning, a perfectly round golden butter bread is waiting for them, warm and fragrant, as though the night itself had baked a little happiness.",
